 the form of enzyme substrates.\nL40: \nL41: ChEBI Ontology\nL42: ---\nL43: \nL44: Text\nL45: \nL46: Tree View\nL47: \nL48: Graph View\nL49: Outgoing Relation(s)\nL50: p-nitrophenyl phenyl phosphonate (【17†CHEBI:91050】) has functional parent 4-nitrophenol (【18†CHEBI:16836】)\nL51: p-nitrophenyl phenyl phosphonate (【17†CHEBI:91050】) has functional parent phenol (【19†CHEBI:15882】)\nL52: p-nitrophenyl phenyl phosphonate (【17†CHEBI:91050】) has role chromogenic compound (【16†CHEBI:75050】)\nL53: p-nitrophenyl phenyl phosphonate (【17†CHEBI:91050】) is a aryl phosphonate (【20†CHEBI:91046】)\nL54: \nL55: IUPAC Name\nL56: ---\nL57: 4-nitrophenyl phenyl phosphonate\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn17view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:55394\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A55394 is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMeSH Browser (https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=D010142)\nciteturn17view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=D010142\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 157\nL0: 【0†googletagmanager†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Search】\nL3:   * 【2†Tree View】\nL4:   * 【3†MeSH on Demand】\nL5:   * 【4†MeSH 2027†meshb-prev.nlm.nih.gov】\nL6:   * 【5†About†www.nlm.nih.gov】\nL7:   * 【6†Suggestions†www.nlm.nih.gov】\nL8:   * 【7†Contact Us†support.nlm.nih.gov】\nL9: # Pactamycin MeSH Descriptor Data 2026\nL10: \nL11:   * Details\nL12:   * Qualifiers\nL13:   * MeSH Tree Structures\nL14:   * Concepts\nL15: MeSH Heading\nL16:     Pactamycin\nL17: Tree Number(s)\nL18:     D02.241.223.100.300.450\nL19:     D02.241.511.390.450\nL20:     D02.455.426.559.389.127.281.450\nL21:     D02.455.426.559.389.657.410.450\nL22: Unique ID\nL23:     D010142\nL24: RDF Unique Identifier\nL25:     【8†http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D010142†id.nlm.nih.gov】\nL26: Scope Note\nL27:     Antibiotic produced by Streptomyces pactum used as an antineoplastic agent. It is also used as a tool in biochemistry because it inhibits certain steps in protein synthesis.\nL28: Pharm Action\nL29:     【9†Antibiotics, Antineoplastic】\nL30: 【10†Protein Synthesis Inhibitors】\nL31: Registry Numbers\nL32:     23668-11-3\nL33: CAS Type 1 Name\nL34:     Benzoic acid, 2-hydroxy-6-methyl-, (5-((3-acetylphenyl)amino)-4-amino-3-(((dimethylamino)carbonyl)amino)-1,2-dihydroxy-3-(1-hydroxyethyl)-2-methylcyclopentyl)methyl ester, (1S-(1alpha,2beta,3alpha,3(R*),4alpha,5beta))-\nL35: Previous Indexing\nL36:     Antibiotics, Antineoplastic (1972-1974)\nL37: Public MeSH Note\nL38:     91; was see under ANTIBIOTICS, ANTINEOPLASTIC 1975-90\nL39: History Note\nL40:     91(75); was see under ANTIBIOTICS, ANTINEOPLASTIC 1975-90\nL41: Date Introduced\nL42:     1991/01/01\nL43: Last Updated\nL44:     2012/07/03\nL45: Allowable Qualifiers\nL46:   * 【11†administration & dosage (AD)】\nL47:   * 【12†adverse effects (AE)】\nL48:   * 【13†agonists (AG)】\nL49:   * 【14†analogs & derivatives (AA)】\nL50:   * 【15†analysis (AN)】\nL51:   * 【16†antagonists & inhibitors (AI)】\nL52:   * 【17†biosynthesis (BI)】\nL53:   * 【18†blood (BL)】\nL54:   * 【19†cerebrospinal fluid (CF)】\nL55:   * 【20†chemical synthesis (CS)】\nL56:   * 【21†chemistry (CH)】\nL57:   * 【22†classification (CL)】\nL58:   * 【23†economics (EC)】\nL59:   * 【24†history (HI)】\nL60:   * 【25†immunology (IM)】\nL61:   * 【26†isolation & purification (IP)】\nL62:   * 【27†metabolism (ME)】\nL63:   * 【28†pharmacokinetics (PK)】\nL64:   * 【29†pharmacology (PD)】\nL65:   * 【30†poisoning (PO)】\nL66:   * 【31†radiation effects (RE)】\nL67:   * 【32†standards (ST)】\nL68:   * 【33†supply & distribution (SD)】\nL69:   * 【34†therapeutic use (TU)】\nL70:   * 【35†toxicity (TO)】\nL71:   * 【36†urine (UR)】\nL72:   * 【37†Organic Chemicals [D02]】\nL73:     * 【38†Carboxylic Acids [D02.241]】\nL7